-- Rollback: Marriage: A Biblical Perspective (marriagechapter1)
UPDATE public.profiles
SET gospel_data = '[{"title":"Marriage: A Biblical Perspective","linkUrl":"https://crosspointechurchmn.snappages.site/media/6vkjfxf/marriage","section":"1","subsections":[{"title":"A Biblical Perspective","content":"","questions":[],"nestedSubsections":[{"title":"Marriage is an institution created by God. Genesis 2:18 It is not good for the m","content":"<p>Marriage is an institution created by God. <br>Genesis 2:18 It is not good for the man to be alone; I will make him a helper suitable for him. <br>Genesis 2:22-23 The LORD God fashioned into a woman the rib which He had taken from the man, and brought her to the man. This is now bone of my bones, And flesh of my flesh; She shall be called Woman, because she was taken out of Man.</p><ol><li><p>The order is significant. God first gives Adam his bride. Then, (and not before) Adam says, “this is now bone of my bones and flesh of my flesh.”.</p></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"Marriage is a covenant relationship joining a man and a woman together for life.","content":"<ol><li><p>A covenant is a formal agreement of legal validity. It is “the word for the most solemn and most binding agreement known to mankind.”<em><sup>1</sup></em><br>Proverbs 2:17 She has abandoned her husband and ignores the covenant she made before God. (NLT) <br>Malachi 2:14 Yet you say, “For what reason?” Because the LORD has been a witness between you and the wife of your youth, against whom you have dealt treacherously, though she is your companion and your wife by covenant. <br>Matthew 19:6 So they are no longer two, but one flesh. What therefore God has joined together let no man separate.</p></li><li><p>When a person sinfully divorces his or her spouse, they are literally undoing the work of God!</p></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"Marriage unites a man and a woman into a “one flesh” relationship. Genesis 2:24","content":"<p>Marriage unites a man and a woman into a “one flesh” relationship. <br>Genesis 2:24 For this reason a man shall leave his father and his mother, and be joined to his wife; and they shall become one flesh.</p><ol><li><p>A “one flesh” relationship implies a sexual relationship, but it means more.</p><ol><li><p>A biblically based definition: Marriage was created by God. In marriage, one man is joined to one woman to become one flesh. They are joined together by a sacred covenant made before God and their union is meant to last for a lifetime.</p></li></ol></li></ol><p></p>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]}],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"Boundaries established by God on marriage.","content":"","questions":[],"nestedSubsections":[{"title":"Marriage is designed for one man to be united with one woman. Genesis 2:24 For t","content":"<p>Marriage is designed for one man to be united with one woman. <br>Genesis 2:24 For this reason a man shall leave his father and his mother, and be joined to his wife; and they shall become one flesh.</p><ol><li><p>Polygamy is the practice of having more than one spouse at one time. <br>Genesis 4:19 Lamech took to himself two wives: the name of the one was Adah, and the name of the other, Zillah.</p><ol><li><p>The New Testament affirms God’s plan for one man with one woman in the state of marriage.</p></li></ol></li><li><p>Homosexuality: a sexual attraction to, and/or sexual relations with, members of the same sex.</p><ol><li><p>Homosexual marriages are inherently forbidden because all forms of homosexuality are forbidden. <br>Leviticus 20:13 If there is a man who lies with a male as those who lie with a woman, both of them have committed a detestable act; they shall surely be put to death. Their bloodguiltiness is upon them. <br>Romans 1:26 For this reason God gave them over to degrading passions; for their women exchanged the natural function for that which is unnatural.</p></li></ol></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"Marriage is meant to last for a lifetime. Matthew 19:6 So they are no longer two","content":"<p>Marriage is meant to last for a lifetime. <br>Matthew 19:6 So they are no longer two, but one flesh. What therefore God has joined together, let no man separate.</p><ol><li><p>Divorce is not in God’s original design for marriage. God hates divorce Mal 2:16).</p><ol><li><p>“Each year in the United States there are about half as many divorces as marriages,”<em><sup>2</sup></em> meaning that roughly half of all marriages end in divorce.</p></li></ol></li><li><p>God has allowed for divorce in two situations. They are sexual immorality, and abandonment by an unbeliever.</p><ol><li><p><strong>Sexual Immorality </strong><br>Matthew 19:9 And I say to you, whoever divorces his wife, except for immorality, and marries another woman commits adultery.</p><ol><li><p>The word “immorality” in this verse comes from the Greek word “porneia” meaning “illicit sexual intercourse.”</p><ol><li><p>This includes adultery, fornication, incest, homosexuality, lesbianism, bestiality, and any other “illicit sexual intercourse.”</p></li></ol></li></ol></li><li><p><strong>Abandonment by an Unbeliever</strong></p><ol><li><p>An unbeliever may decide to leave a marriage for any reason and many times there is nothing the believer can do to change their mind. When this happens, the Bible allows for divorce. <br>1 Corinthians 7:15 Yet if the unbelieving one leaves, let him leave; the brother or the sister is not under bondage in such cases, but God has called us to peace.</p></li><li><p>If the unbeliever should divorce, the believer is free to remarry; she is “not under bondage.”</p></li></ol></li></ol></li></ol><p></p>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]}],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"The Purposes of Marriage","content":"","questions":[],"nestedSubsections":[{"title":"A Purpose of Marriage is Legitimate Sexual Fulfillment Ephesians 5:31 . . . And","content":"<p>A Purpose of Marriage is Legitimate Sexual Fulfillment <br>Ephesians 5:31 . . . And the two shall become one flesh.</p><ol><li><p>Sexual relations within the bounds of marriage are honorable and pleasing to God. <br>Hebrews 13:4 Marriage is to be held in honor among all, and the marriage bed is to be undefiled; for fornicators and adulterers God will judge. <br>Proverbs 5:19 As a loving hind and a graceful doe, Let her breasts satisfy you at all times; Be exhilarated always with her love.</p></li><li><p>Marriage authorizes the sexual relationship between a man and a woman and is a God-given gift to keep us from sexual sin.</p></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"A Purpose of Marriage is Procreation Genesis 1:28 God blessed them; and God said","content":"<p>A Purpose of Marriage is Procreation <br>Genesis 1:28 God blessed them; and God said to them, “Be fruitful and multiply, and fill the earth, and subdue it; and rule over the fish of the sea and over the birds of the sky and over every living thing that moves on the earth.”</p><ol><li><p>A. Calvin states, “Adam with his wife was formed for the production of offspring, in order that men might replenish the earth.”<em><sup>3</sup></em></p></li><li><p>In the era of the Old Testament, if a woman could not have a child she felt disgraced. When Rachel couldn’t bear children she said to Jacob, “Give me children, or else I die” (Gen 30:1). <br>Psalms 127:4-5 Like arrows in the hand of a warrior, So are the children of one''s youth. How blessed is the man whose quiver is full of them; They will not be ashamed When they speak with their enemies in the gate.</p></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"A Purpose of Marriage is to Become Like Christ 1 Corinthians 7:28 But if you mar","content":"<p>A Purpose of Marriage is to Become Like Christ <br>1 Corinthians 7:28 But if you marry, you have not sinned; and if a virgin marries, she has not sinned. Yet such will have trouble in this life, and I am trying to spare you.</p><ol><li><p>It is impossible for two sinners to be united together in perfect harmony; conflicts and problems will arise. <br>Romans 8:28-29 And we know that God causes all things to work together for good to those who love God, to those who are called according to His purpose. For those whom He foreknew, He also predestined to become conformed to the image of His Son, so that He would be the firstborn among many brethren;</p></li><li><p>Every trial or conflict that comes into a marriage brings an opportunity for a spouse to deny the flesh and become more like Christ. Each time the flesh is denied, and God’s Word is obeyed, that spouse grows in his or her Christian maturity.</p></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"A Purpose of Marriage is to be a Picture of Christ and the Church Ephesians 5:31","content":"<p>A Purpose of Marriage is to be a Picture of Christ and the Church <br>Ephesians 5:31-32 For this reason a man shall leave his father and mother and shall be joined to his wife, and the two shall become one flesh. This mystery is great; but I am speaking with reference to Christ and the church.”</p><ol><li><p>Jay Adams states, “When a husband and wife approximate the proper relationship of Christ to His church, they bear a good witness to the saving grace of Christ. When they fail, they bring shame on the name of the Lord.”<em><sup>4</sup></em></p></li><li><p>When a wife lovingly submits to her husband as unto the Lord, she is demonstrating the submissive love the church is to have for Christ.</p></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"A Purpose of Marriage is Companionship","content":"<ol><li><p>The primary purpose for which God created marriage was to deal with man’s loneliness. Genesis 2:18 Then the LORD God said, “It is not good for the man to be alone; I will make him a helper suitable for him.”</p></li><li><p>Jay Adams states, “Companionship, therefore, is the essence of marriage.”<em><sup>5</sup></em></p></li><li><p>God designed marriage to take care of loneliness, and when a husband and wife become close and intimate companions, they glorify God. Marriage is primarily a covenant of companionship!</p></li></ol><ol><li><p>Jay E. Adams, Solving Marriage Problems: Biblical Solutions for Christian Counselors, 23-24.</p></li><li><p>Norman L. Geisler, Christian Ethics; Options and Issues (Grand Rapids: Baker, 1989), 277.</p></li><li><p>Williamson, Westminster Confession of Faith, 236.</p></li><li><p>Adams, Solving Marriage Problems, 3.</p></li><li><p>Adams, Marriage, Divorce, Remarriage, 8.</p></li></ol><p></p>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]}],"scriptureReferences":[]}],"linkDescription":"Watch the recording of this content."},{"title":"Homework","section":"2","subsections":[{"title":"Homework Questions","content":"<p>Complete the exercises below and save your answers.</p>","questions":[{"id":"q-1762815699165-cmazjtvcl","question":"Memory Verse: Matthew 19:6 So they are no longer two, but one flesh. What therefore God has joined together, let no man separate.","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:01:39.165Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815727530-636ay6o5j","question":"<p>Scripture: Read Genesis 2 with your spouse. </p><ul><li><p>Discuss what it says and answer the following question: </p><ul><li><p>Is marriage a man-made institution, or was it created by God? </p></li><li><p>Why is this significant?</p></li></ul></li></ul><p></p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:02:07.530Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815743329-368lco85v","question":"Review and discuss this lesson with your spouse.","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:02:23.329Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815771780-km1fv8sxs","question":"Pray daily to love your spouse and to be a better companion.","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:02:51.780Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815788546-a7zpmi1z2","question":"Attend Church together.","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:03:08.546Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815849312-qrorii0ba","question":"<p>Application</p><ul><li><p>Do 3 “above the norm, out of the ordinary” kind acts to your spouse this week.</p></li><li><p>Record what you did.</p></li><li><p>Make a list of what makes you feel lonely in your marriage and share it with your spouse.</p></li><li><p>When you get your spouse’s list, do what you can, based on what he/she wrote, to eliminate his/her loneliness.</p></li><li><p>Record what you did.</p></li><li><p>Do something on this list every day!</p></li></ul><p></p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:04:09.312Z","maxLength":2000}],"nestedSubsections":[]}]}]'::jsonb, updated_at = NOW()
WHERE slug = 'marriagechapter1';
